  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "y3z6ld8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. MEANING OF PUBLIC FINANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Public Finance deals with government income, spending, debt, and financial administration.",
        "The Finance Commission is constituted every 5 years under Article 280 to recommend tax devolution formula and grants-in-aid.",
        "The 15th Finance Commission recommended a 41% vertical devolution share to States, with Income Distance receiving the highest horizontal weight (45%).",
        "The FRBM 2018 target caps combined public debt at 60% of GDP (40% Centre and 20% States).",
        "Food subsidy is the largest explicit subsidy in India."
      ],
      "id": "qsm6qr0"
    },
    {
