    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Public Finance refers to the study of government revenue, expenditure, public debt and financial administration. It deals with how the government manages its income and spending.",
      "id": "rfah4c2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Main components: Public Revenue, Public Expenditure, Public Debt and Financial Administration.",
      "id": "x0z5qcz"
    },
    {
      "id": "25x7qcn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. PUBLIC REVENUE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Public Revenue is the income earned by the government.",
      "id": "zb5opma"
    },
