    {
      "id": "mgboosg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. PUBLIC DEBT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Public Debt refers to total borrowings of the government.",
      "id": "bka14vi"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Internal Debt – Borrowings within country (bonds, treasury bills)<br/>• External Debt – Borrowings from foreign sources<br/>",
      "id": "px4jgvs"
    },
    {
      "id": "nnzomqc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. FISCAL FEDERALISM IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "India follows federal structure of finance. Financial powers are divided between Centre and States under the Constitution.",
      "id": "ib9i6g4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Finance Commission (Article 280) recommends distribution of taxes between Centre and States.",
      "id": "wrrkulz"
    },
    {
      "id": "cso80mo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. FINANCE COMMISSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Public Finance refers to the study of government revenue, expenditure, public debt and financial administration.",
      "id": "jvrrbab"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Constituted every 5 years under Article 280 of the Constitution.",
      "id": "kabaqxx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Functions:<br/>• Recommend tax devolution formula<br/>• Recommend grants-in-aid to states<br/>",
      "id": "8qsa4e9"
    },
    {
