    {
      "id": "g71fry8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. PUBLIC DEBT SUSTAINABILITY ANALYSIS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Debt sustainability refers to government's ability to service debt without crisis.",
      "id": "jxm1og5"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 280 is frequently asked as the Constitutional basis for forming the Finance Commission every 5 years.",
        "Income Distance carries the highest weightage (45%) in the 15th Finance Commission horizontal devolution formula.",
        "Under FRBM 2018, remember the target split: 40% for the Centre and 20% for the States.",
        "Revenue expenditure does not lead to the creation of assets."
      ],
      "id": "3w9u8zw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Key Indicators:<br/>• Debt-to-GDP Ratio<br/>• Interest Payments / Revenue Receipts<br/>• Fiscal Deficit as % of GDP<br/>",
      "id": "1kqtc5l"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "FRBM 2018 Target: Combined Debt = 60% of GDP (40% Centre, 20% States).",
      "id": "c2167at"
    },
